The '''Moyn'''<ref name="TCWE">''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars: Character Encyclopedia - Join the Battle!]]''</ref> were a [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] of [[Color|brown]] [[Hair|furred]] [[humanoid]]s that inhabited [[the galaxy]] during the [[Clone Wars]]<ref name="Gone with a Trace" /> and the [[Imperial Era|reign]] of the [[Galactic Empire]]. They had two protruding [[eye]]s with horizontally closing eyelids, and several small tentacle-like appendages that surrounded their [[mouth]]. The [[species]] was capable of speaking [[Galactic Basic Standard]] and could breathe unfiltered [[Clouzon-36]] [[gas]].<ref name="The Call" /> Members of the species included [[Level 1313]] moneylender [[Pintu Son-El]]<ref name="Gone with a Trace" /> and the bad-tempered [[Mining Guild]] [[boss]] [[Yushyn]], who operated an [[Asteroid Belt Gas Refinery]]<ref name="The Call" /> in [[3 BBY]].<ref name="The Call date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of "[[The Call]]" to [[3 BBY]].</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:Yushyn_original_concept.png|thumb|left|150px|Yushyn's design was based on concept art drawn by Ralph McQuarrie.]]
The Moyn first appeared in "[[The Call]]," the thirteenth episode in the [[Star Wars Rebels Season Two|second season]] of the ''[[Star Wars Rebels]]'' television show.<ref name="The Call" /> The design for the species was based on a piece of alien bounty hunter concept art drawn by [[Ralph McQuarrie]] for [[Star Wars: Episode V The Empire Strikes Back|''Star Wars'': Episode V ''The Empire Strikes Back'']]. Concept art of Yushyn for the ''Rebels'' episode was produced by artist [[JP Balmet]].<ref name="SW-The Call Episode Guide &#124; Star Wars Rebels">{{SW|url=series/star-wars-rebels/the-call-episode-guide|text="The Call" Episode Guide &#124; Star Wars Rebels}}</ref> The species was originally created for unfinished episodes of ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'', with the character of Pintu Son-El.<ref name="SWYouTube-Ahsoka's Untold Tales Panel &#124; Star Wars Celebration Europe 2016">{{SWYouTube|lS4sclln5J4|Ahsoka's Untold Tales Panel &#124; Star Wars Celebration Europe 2016}}</ref> Son-El would eventually appear in the revived [[The Clone Wars: Season Seven|seventh season]] of the series, in the [[2020]] episode "[[Gone with a Trace]]."<ref name="Gone with a Trace">{{TCW|Gone with a Trace}}</ref> The species was named after [[Bobby Moynihan]],<ref name="Bobby">{{YouTube|video=9vP0b5AUZAI|text=Bobby Moynihan: Interview -The Big Thing|channel=UC7BZTnHihGgs7XZmXEBirjA|name=Kristian Harloff}}</ref> who voiced Son-El in the episode.<ref name="Gone with a Trace" />

